        "code": {
          "text": "Lumbar facet joint syndrome / osteoarthritis; chronic condition with current mild-to-moderate flare"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Low back pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Longstanding intermittent pain localized to the lumbar region, with no radiation. Current flare began gradually about 3 weeks ago without trauma. Pain is 4/10 at baseline and up to 7/10 after prolonged sitting or driving; worsened by extension and twisting, and improved with heat, gentle stretches, and distraction. More noticeable at night when quiet."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Back pain red-flag symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies leg weakness, numbness or paraesthesia, saddle anaesthesia, bowel or bladder symptoms, fever, weight loss, and night sweats."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Function with back pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Still managing activities of daily living and working, with more breaks; employer is flexible. Walks the dog in short walks. No current physiotherapy; last physiotherapy was more than 12 months ago."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood, coping, and sleep"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Frustrated with chronic pain but coping okay. Denies depression and anxiety. No sleep issues other than waking due to pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance and respiratory observation by video"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Well appearing, no apparent distress, speaking in full sentences. No obvious pallor or cyanosis. Respiratory rate visually normal; no audible wheeze or cough."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neurological observation by video"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert and oriented, normal affect, coherent speech, moves all limbs spontaneously, and no obvious focal deficit."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Musculoskeletal observation by video"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Rose independently from a chair but slowly, with mild stiffness on straightening. Walked a few steps in the room with a non-antalgic gait. No obvious deformity."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
